  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "The University of Debrecen is a public research university in Debrecen, Hungary, and the oldest continuously operating institution of higher education in Hungary, with roots dating back to 1538 as the Calvinist College of Debrecen. It was reorganised as a Hungarian Royal University in 1912 and took its modern form through a 2000 merger of several Debrecen institutions into a single 13-faculty university.",
      "With approximately 30,000 students and nearly 6,000 international students from over 100 countries, the University of Debrecen is one of the largest and most international universities in Central Europe. English-language instruction has been offered since 1886, and today the university runs more than 80 degree programmes fully taught in English across 13 faculties: Medicine, Dentistry, Pharmacy, Engineering, Informatics, Economics and Business, Law, Music, Agriculture, Science and Technology, Humanities, Public Health, and Child and Special Needs Education.",
      "The university is particularly well-known internationally for General Medicine (MD), Dentistry (DMD) and Pharmacy (PharmD) programmes taught entirely in English, which are recognised across the EU, UK and many other jurisdictions. The Faculty of Medicine teaching hospital (Clinical Centre) is the largest in Hungary, and Debrecen also hosts Komondor, Hungary's largest supercomputer, supporting research in life sciences, physics and informatics.",
      "Campuses are spread across the city of Debrecen — the historic main building sits in the leafy Nagyerdő (Great Forest) park, with additional sites on Kassai Road (law, economics, IT, engineering) and Böszörményi Road (agriculture). Students study, live and socialise within walking distance of one of Hungary's most affordable and student-friendly cities, with strong international community life centred around the Auguszta and Nagyerdő districts."
    ],
    "paragraphsRu": [
      "University of Debrecen — государственный исследовательский университет в Дебрецене, Венгрия, и старейший непрерывно работающий вуз страны: корни — Calvinist College of Debrecen 1538 года. Реорганизован в Hungarian Royal University в 1912 году, современная структура — после слияния 2000 года в единый университет из 13 факультетов.",
      "30 000 студентов, около 6 000 международных из 100+ стран — один из крупнейших и самых интернациональных университетов Центральной Европы. Преподавание на английском — с 1886 года; сегодня 80+ программ полностью на английском по 13 факультетам: Medicine, Dentistry, Pharmacy, Engineering, Informatics, Economics and Business, Law, Music, Agriculture, Science and Technology, Humanities, Public Health, Child and Special Needs Education.",
      "В мире университет известен прежде всего англоязычными программами General Medicine (MD), Dentistry (DMD) и Pharmacy (PharmD) — дипломы признаются в EU, UK и большинстве других юрисдикций. Учебная клиника Faculty of Medicine (Clinical Centre) — крупнейшая университетская в Венгрии; здесь же работает Komondor — самый мощный суперкомпьютер страны.",
      "Кампусы — по всему Дебрецену: исторический корпус в парке Nagyerdő, Kassai Road (law, economics, IT, engineering) и Böszörményi Road (agriculture). Дебрецен — один из самых доступных и student-friendly городов Венгрии; интернациональная community сконцентрирована вокруг районов Auguszta и Nagyerdő."
